After Frakir, Derek suggested that he's looking for more helms/gloves/
shields for Sporkhack, rather than new artifacts. Lots of fun - came
up with following list. Tried not to make too overpowered, esp. with
specific advantages for one character class:

GLOVES:
1. Throwing gloves: Give increased projectile range and add (1 +
enchantment) to damage or something.
Possibly extra projectile for multishot. Yeah, puny compared to
gauntlets of power, but early characters might still like them. I
guess they're the "kicking boots" of the glove world. However,
increased range may *not* be a good thing if you actually want to
retrieve those daggers. :)
2. Electrified gloves: Give a small shock bonus to damage attacks,
gloved or with iron/silver weapon, with possible ring/wand explosion.
Provide shock resistance. Hey, may be weak compared to GoP, but shock
resist could save life from vortices, wand of lightning.

Problems I see: these both seem like poor man's GoP, unless the
throwing gloves have a multishot advantage. Good news is an extra
multishot would give more benefit to priests and other characters with
limited range capability - 2 shots vs. one is way better than four
shots vs three! Also, in late game when strength at max, a small
damage bonus *on top of strength* might be desirable.

HATS:
1. Tinfoil hat.
Massively hinders spellcasting. Reduces damage from psi-bolts and MMF
telepathy attacks.
2. Scuba helmet.
Acts like an amulet of magical breathing, and provides AC 2, but
rather heavy (oxygen tanks?).
3. Miner's cap: Acts as light source, AC 2. Chance of dwarves having
it. Not sure whether charging necessary.
4. Helm of psionic focus (upgraded helm of telepathy)
Maybe it's an upgraded helm of telepathy, since the helm of telepathy
is so rare to begin with and has such a weak effect when so many
artifacts provide ESP. Or maybe comined/mishmashed with tinfoil hat.
Confers telepathy, and allows a psionic blast dealing damage on par
with force bolt when (a)pplied. Targets specific monster, not group.
Hey, it's a weak attack, and only affects one monster, but it *is*
ranged!

SHIELDS:
1. Shield of dreams (unidentified "night-blue shield").
When worn, provides sleep resist and possibly free action ("Your
shield glimmers like the night sky and you feel lucid again" if sleep
attacked, and shield identified in process). When wielded, provides a
sleep attack, respecting magic resistance of monsters. Hey, it's a
shield of DREAMS, right?
2. Shield of reflection:
Why the hell doesn't this give silver damage to monks? I assume that a
monk wearing this shield *is* holding it when he bashes monsters. Oh
well, would probably unbalance monks.

